.TH lsf.task 5 "Volclava"
.SH NAME
lsf.task \- task eligibility and resource requirements
.SH DESCRIPTION
The task configuration defines remote-task resource requirements and a local-task
list used by the task eligibility library. It does not define batch queues.
.PP
On first use, the library reads the following readable files in order:
.IP 1. 3
LSF_CONFDIR/lsf.task
.IP 2. 3
LSF_CONFDIR/lsf.task.clustername, if the cluster name is available
.IP 3. 3
$HOME/.lsftask
.PP
Later entries can replace or remove earlier entries in the same task list.
The local and remote lists are separate. At least one task file must be read
successfully for task-list initialization to succeed.
.SH FORMAT
Entries appear in sections delimited by either
.B Begin RemoteTasks
and
.BR "End RemoteTasks" ,
or
.B Begin LocalTasks
and
.BR "End LocalTasks" .
Section keywords are case-insensitive. Task names are case-sensitive.
.PP
Each entry adds a task unless prefixed with a minus sign, which removes it
from that section's list. A plus sign explicitly adds an entry. The sign may
be attached to the entry or separated by whitespace. Remote-task entries
may be enclosed in double quotes to include spaces in resource requirements.
.PP
A remote-task entry has the form
.IR task/resource_requirement .
The resource requirement is optional. Adding an existing task replaces its
previous resource requirement; an entry without a requirement clears it.
.PP
By default, the first slash separates the task name from its resource
requirement, and eligibility lookup uses the basename of the requested task.
If LSF_TRS is set, its first character is the separator and lookup uses the
task string as supplied. Use a nonempty separator value when setting LSF_TRS.
.SH ELIGIBILITY
In local mode, a task is eligible only if it appears in RemoteTasks.
In remote mode, a task is eligible unless it appears in LocalTasks.
When an eligible task also appears in RemoteTasks, its configured resource
requirement is returned. A missing requirement is returned as an empty string.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
Begin RemoteTasks
gcc/cpu>=0
"compress/order[cpu:mem]"
\- obsolete_task
End RemoteTasks

Begin LocalTasks
local_only_task
End LocalTasks
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.B LSF_CONFDIR/lsf.task
Global task configuration.
.TP
.B LSF_CONFDIR/lsf.task.clustername
Cluster-specific task configuration.
.TP
.B $HOME/.lsftask
Per-user task configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
lsf.conf(5)
